$GBDB_ROOT/<db>/$GBDB_SUBDIR/ now links to the metadata and color files in
$here.  That directory needs to stay where it is; removing it would
break the tracks.

Those $GBDB_ROOT files still need to go out to production.  They are listed one
per line in $here/%(gbdbManifestName)s.  They are symlinks, so
whatever pushes them has to follow the link rather than copy it.
"
if [ "$MISSING_COUNT" -gt 0 ]; then
    mailBody="$mailBody
When these files were built, $MISSING_COUNT bigDataUrl(s) did not resolve on the
mirror under %(mirrorUrl)s/data/.  They are listed one per line,
with the reason, in $here/%(missingName)s.  Each one is a broken
track, so fix the mirror or drop those stanzas before they reach production.
"
else
    mailBody="$mailBody
Every bigDataUrl was found on the mirror when these files were built.
"
fi
if [ -n "$newDbs" ]; then
    mailBody="$mailBody
These assemblies had no methbase2.ra before this update:"
    for db in $newDbs; do
        mailBody="$mailBody
    $db (${dbPath[$db]})"
